From 25ea3b4b9ba8100fd9c460116cca837c534979c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 12:58:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] httpd: Reaper_Wireless - raise the radio-unit ceiling to
 quad-band

RWIFI_MAXUNIT was 2 (written on the tri-band RT-BE96U), which made the
wireless diagnostics page enumerate units 0..2 only and reject unit 3 in
the capture allowlist. On quad-band models (GT-BE98/GT-BE98_PRO) that hid
the 4th radio - the 6 GHz radio, precisely the one the GT-BE98 field
report is about. Raise the ceiling to 3: rwifi_ifname() already skips
units whose wlN_ifname nvram is absent, so tri-band boards are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/httpd/web.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/httpd/web.c b/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
index f17e0acf577..cfd98884ed5 100644
--- a/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
+++ b/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
@@ -22002,7 +22002,7 @@ do_reaper_traffic_cgi(char *url, FILE *stream)
 #define RWIFI_DIR	"/tmp/reaper_wifi"
 #define RWIFI_CSV	RWIFI_DIR "/cap.csv"
 #define RWIFI_RUN	RWIFI_DIR "/run"
-#define RWIFI_MAXUNIT	2
+#define RWIFI_MAXUNIT	3	/* quad-band ceiling; absent units have no wlN_ifname and are skipped */
 
 static int rwifi_ifname(int unit, char *buf, size_t blen)
 {
-- 
